{ P312: every product by a constant takes its recipe, the remainder's
  multiply back and the general path included. x mod C and x * C for
  the constants of the golden programs (and some negative ones for the
  product): as a function's result, from register variables of a
  loop's region (the constant on the right, on the left and in place),
  and through a global, on edge values of the integer; the products
  stay in range. On amd64 a product the recipe of Go's costs makes
  cheaper is leas, adds and shifts, and the remainder subtracts the
  quotient's recipe; on arm64 the same where the processor -tune names
  makes the recipe cheaper than MUL or MSUB. scripts/check_modconst.py
  reads the routines M, Loop and Glob of each constant. Written by a
  script; the answers are Python's. }
program modconst;

var
  xs: array[0..15] of Integer;
  ys: array[0..7] of Integer;
  g: Integer;

function M3(x: Integer): Integer;
begin
  Result := x mod 3;
end;

